1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:09,850
Logs are the building's CCTV. Attackers leave footprints: many failed logins, odd times, strange addresses.

2
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:16,025
Defenders read logs to spot attacks early, before damage is done.

3
00:00:17,730 --> 00:00:26,380
Fifty failed logins from one address in one minute, then one success. That is a password-guessing attack that worked.

4
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:33,080
Lock the account, block the address, reset the password, and check what was accessed.

5
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:43,705
Count failures per address, look for logins from new countries, and watch for requests full of quote marks and script tags.

6
00:00:44,410 --> 00:00:48,785
Understanding attacks makes you a far better defender.

